INCLUDE include.ink

->START

===START===

You find yourself holding a flat stone tablet, its surface covered in crude but colorful pictures. The images seem to show some kind of magical process - there's drawings of shiny things, wavy lines that might be magic, and what looks like a really angry wizard pointing at stuff.

Being an orc, you can't read the squiggly symbols, but the pictures? Those you can understand. Sort of.

This side of the stone shows the first part of... something. Maybe it's about making things more killy?

+ [Turn da rok over]->SecondSide
+ [Put da rok down]->END

===SecondSide===
#illustration: gs_enchant_table_2

You flip the stone tablet over. The other side has more pictures! This one shows the next part of the process. There's more shiny bits, some glowy effects, and what definitely looks like a proper choppa at the end - but it's got magic sparkles on it!

You nod sagely. You're pretty sure you understand now. Magic makes things better. You knew that already, but it's nice to have it confirmed by a rock with pictures.

+ [Turn da rok back]->START
+ [Put da rok down]->END
